WEBVTT

00:22.120 --> 00:23.020
Brother...

00:43.270 --> 00:54.360
<b>The Reincarnation of
the Strongest Exorcist in Another World</b>

01:58.990 --> 01:59.730
Hey.

02:00.580 --> 02:01.830
Wait, wait.

02:01.830 --> 02:03.140
I'm not here to fight.

02:03.570 --> 02:06.560
And you're not especially good 
with that dagger, are you?

02:06.560 --> 02:07.520
How...?

02:07.810 --> 02:10.280
You didn't seem too satisfied with it.

02:10.280 --> 02:13.230
You're more accustomed to using
heavier weapons, aren't you?

02:14.200 --> 02:15.830
This place is nice and quiet.

02:16.280 --> 02:18.770
It's a shame it's such a clear sky, though.

02:19.540 --> 02:21.450
What's wrong with a clear sky?

02:21.450 --> 02:25.580
I prefer it when there's at 
least one cloud obscuring the moon.

02:25.870 --> 02:28.390
There's no elegance in a 
moon that's too bright.

02:28.390 --> 02:30.930
Especially if there's not one, but two.

02:30.930 --> 02:32.190
Elegance?

02:32.190 --> 02:34.300
And of course there's two moons...

02:35.590 --> 02:36.790
You're strange.

02:36.790 --> 02:39.430
Why did you follow me, if not to fight me?

02:40.080 --> 02:42.030
I came to talk.

02:42.030 --> 02:47.390
Tell me what's troubling you, 
and I might change my mind.

02:47.810 --> 02:50.640
Talk? After what just happened?

02:50.640 --> 02:51.850
You're crazy.

02:52.400 --> 02:55.820
But you didn't try to kill me.

02:56.710 --> 02:58.740
Nor the person who interrupted us.

02:58.980 --> 03:02.960
You looked like you were 
trying to kill him...

03:02.960 --> 03:05.240
I didn't plan on it.

03:05.600 --> 03:11.550
I just wanted to injure you, 
so you'd forfeit the fight tomorrow.

03:11.550 --> 03:14.170
You went a little far for that.

03:14.170 --> 03:17.690
Sure, I was planning to take 
two or three of your limbs...

03:17.690 --> 03:20.690
Could you have healed yourself 
even if I had hurt you?

03:20.690 --> 03:21.710
Who knows?

03:22.170 --> 03:26.420
But still... if I fought 
for real, I wouldn't lose.

03:26.420 --> 03:28.350
There's a reason I can't lose.

03:28.740 --> 03:30.710
Please, forfeit.

03:30.710 --> 03:33.080
I won't be able to hold back against you.

03:33.080 --> 03:35.050
And I don't want anyone else to die.

03:35.050 --> 03:35.730
So...

03:35.730 --> 03:37.690
You're here in Amyu's place.

03:38.690 --> 03:45.410
Your job is to win here and become a 
fake hero to draw the demons' attention.

03:45.410 --> 03:46.750
You knew?

03:46.750 --> 03:51.260
I did, yeah. But there's another reason 
why this is so important to you, I think.

03:51.260 --> 03:54.710
Tell me, and maybe I will forfeit.

03:55.800 --> 03:58.880
There's one thing you're wrong about.

03:59.340 --> 04:03.300
My job is to be killed by the 
swordsman with the evil eye,

04:04.560 --> 04:08.350
to make the demons think the hero is dead.

04:08.840 --> 04:12.060
<i>So Kyle was sent here, too?</i>

04:12.470 --> 04:13.950
The Rugrock Merchants Association

04:13.950 --> 04:18.000
takes slave children with potential 
and turns them into mercenaries.

04:18.000 --> 04:20.230
Both Kyle and I were trained by them.

04:20.620 --> 04:22.540
<i>I thought so.</i>

04:22.540 --> 04:25.920
<i>That explains where she 
learned to fight like that.</i>

04:25.920 --> 04:29.880
The most important thing for the
Merchants Association in this tournament

04:29.880 --> 04:32.440
is testing whether Kyle has 
become a perfect mercenary.

04:32.440 --> 04:33.510
Testing?

04:33.510 --> 04:34.450
Yes.

04:34.450 --> 04:36.790
To make you one of their mercenaries,

04:37.110 --> 04:41.000
they open a hole in your skull 
and implant magic in your brain.

04:41.000 --> 04:46.000
Then you cease to feel any 
fear, anger, or hesitation.

04:46.000 --> 04:49.230
You become a perfect mercenary, 
who obeys any order.

04:49.230 --> 04:53.360
In exchange, though, you lose 
feelings like joy and sorrow,

04:53.360 --> 04:55.290
and become a different person.

04:56.770 --> 05:00.570
The children who are gathered by the 
Merchants Association to become mercenaries

05:00.570 --> 05:02.660
are put into groups of 
four at the training camp.

05:02.660 --> 05:05.480
You train together and 
spend all your time together.

05:06.170 --> 05:08.990
You all tell each other to do your best...

05:08.990 --> 05:14.780
And the grown-ups tell you all the time to 
help each other and care for each other.

05:15.840 --> 05:19.400
But only one of the four 
is given the surgery.

05:20.150 --> 05:25.550
And only by killing your three 
friends can you become a mercenary.

05:25.940 --> 05:27.220
That's the test you have to pass.

05:27.990 --> 05:31.000
I was supposed to be just killed, 
but instead they can make money off of me,

05:31.000 --> 05:34.010
and use the tournament as 
a way to make Kyle famous.

05:34.010 --> 05:35.390
So you're...

05:35.780 --> 05:40.860
The last of the three 
friends Kyle has to kill.

05:42.860 --> 05:46.510
And that's why you decided to 
make it all the way to the finals?

05:47.130 --> 05:49.190
So he can kill you?

05:49.190 --> 05:50.020
No.

05:50.470 --> 05:52.080
Then, why?

05:52.080 --> 05:55.760
I don't care about the hero, the test,
 the academy, or the Merchants Association.

05:55.760 --> 05:59.290
I have to kill Kyle in the finals.

05:59.640 --> 06:01.610
He killed my brother...

06:01.610 --> 06:03.730
One of the others that died was my brother.

06:04.580 --> 06:07.220
So I have to get revenge.

06:07.710 --> 06:09.280
You're lying.

06:09.280 --> 06:11.390
Kyle's your brother, isn't he?

06:12.120 --> 06:15.000
Your red hair... that's just dye, isn't it?

06:15.000 --> 06:18.100
And you have the same color eyes as him.

06:18.610 --> 06:20.900
He's your brother, isn't he?

06:21.820 --> 06:23.340
You know everything, don't you?

06:26.600 --> 06:29.140
Before he got the surgery, he said...

06:30.480 --> 06:33.380
If I ever stop being me,

06:33.380 --> 06:36.370
I want you to set me free.

06:38.740 --> 06:40.920
I'm counting on you, Mabel.

06:42.320 --> 06:44.740
He's not my brother anymore.

06:44.740 --> 06:47.300
My brother wouldn't kill innocents.

06:48.080 --> 06:54.530
But if any part of my brother is still 
inside that man, I want to set him free.

06:54.530 --> 06:57.190
Do you think you can beat Kyle?

06:57.190 --> 07:00.210
I don't know, but I have to.

07:00.210 --> 07:02.520
This is something only I can do.

07:02.810 --> 07:04.840
All that's left for me is death.

07:04.840 --> 07:07.780
Whether I win, or lose and run away,

07:07.780 --> 07:10.100
the Merchants Association will kill me.

07:10.100 --> 07:11.600
So, at the very least, 
I can do this for him...

07:11.600 --> 07:13.200
I changed my mind.

07:13.550 --> 07:15.870
I'll defeat Kyle in the finals.

07:16.290 --> 07:17.410
Why?

07:17.680 --> 07:20.200
There's no need for you to die.

07:20.200 --> 07:21.460
This is wrong.

07:21.460 --> 07:23.510
What do you know about anything?

07:23.510 --> 07:25.460
It's too late for empty words!

07:25.800 --> 07:27.120
I'm different!

07:27.120 --> 07:28.970
I'm not like those empty-headed rich kids,

07:28.970 --> 07:31.800
or the hero who grew up 
loved by everyone, or you!

07:32.290 --> 07:35.140
I don't have a choice! 
What am I supposed to do?

07:35.140 --> 07:36.860
Go back to the academy.

07:36.860 --> 07:39.780
There's no way they'll let me do that!

07:39.780 --> 07:44.310
Don't worry. I won't let anybody 
touch you as long as I'm there.

07:44.310 --> 07:47.120
Y-You can't...

07:47.120 --> 07:48.030
I can.

07:48.450 --> 07:51.570
I'm the strongest.

07:52.940 --> 07:54.200
And...

07:54.200 --> 07:59.160
If your brother wants anything, 
I'm sure it's not death.

07:59.680 --> 08:04.530
It's for his sister to be free.

08:06.090 --> 08:07.250
Thanks...

08:07.990 --> 08:11.460
But tomorrow, I'm going to use my full power.

08:11.460 --> 08:13.090
And I'll beat you.

08:13.330 --> 08:18.160
Sure. For my part, I'll prove 
to you that I'm the strongest.

08:18.160 --> 08:19.140
All right.

08:21.350 --> 08:26.080
<i>Even in this life, he still can't 
resist helping people in trouble...</i>

08:30.440 --> 08:33.530
It's time for the second 
match of the semifinals!

08:33.530 --> 08:39.120
Kyle has already secured his place in the 
finals, but who will be his opponent?

08:39.630 --> 08:43.710
Mabel Crane from Lodonea Magic Academy,

08:44.000 --> 08:47.080
or her classmate, Seika Lamprogue?

08:47.660 --> 08:49.880
Is that your usual weapon?

08:50.150 --> 08:51.800
I'm done pretending to be the hero.

08:52.230 --> 08:55.310
Now I can see your true strength.

08:55.310 --> 08:56.470
You think I'm not strong?

08:56.800 --> 08:58.530
That's not true.

08:58.530 --> 09:00.890
I just want to know how 
strong you really are.

09:00.890 --> 09:05.980
A noble kid who's been spoiled 
his whole life can't beat me.

09:05.980 --> 09:08.810
Who will be the victor?

09:09.130 --> 09:10.770
Let the match begin!

09:20.680 --> 09:23.070
<i>She's as fast as someone 
with a one-handed sword.</i>

09:23.070 --> 09:25.120
<i>Did she use gravity magic to lighten it?</i>

09:25.120 --> 09:26.260
<i>Phase of sunlight.</i>

09:26.260 --> 09:27.540
<i>Spell of Internal Release.</i>

09:29.300 --> 09:30.210
<i>Interesting.</i>

09:35.520 --> 09:36.870
Phase of wood.

09:36.870 --> 09:38.140
Spell of Binding Vines.

09:41.100 --> 09:42.460
This can't stop me!

09:46.640 --> 09:48.900
Phase of sunlight. Spell of Falling Fruit.

09:49.330 --> 09:51.570
That made it a thousand times heavier.

09:51.570 --> 09:55.180
Phase of wood and metal. 
Spell of Mercury Binding Vines.

09:56.190 --> 09:57.820
It won't work twice!

10:00.460 --> 10:01.490
I can break free...

10:02.140 --> 10:06.660
These vines are made of mercury. 
They're a lot heavier.

10:07.440 --> 10:10.400
You'll never be able to lift that...

10:10.400 --> 10:11.590
Sure I will.

10:11.870 --> 10:14.300
Phase of shadow. Spell of Floating Leaves.

10:15.770 --> 10:19.360
You can't hurt me with that light ax.

10:19.360 --> 10:21.750
I'm not going to hurt you.

10:22.910 --> 10:25.470
I just need to win the fight.

10:26.450 --> 10:27.820
The match is over!

10:27.820 --> 10:30.440
Seika Lamprogue wins by judges' vote!

10:30.440 --> 10:34.900
Mabel had the advantage early in the match, 
but she lost it almost immediately!

10:35.180 --> 10:38.550
Or was that part of his plan?

10:38.550 --> 10:42.570
The amazing Seika Lamprogue 
will be going to the finals!

10:42.930 --> 10:46.300
It's okay. Leave Kyle to me.

10:49.330 --> 10:51.210
<i>You're definitely strong.</i>

10:52.500 --> 10:53.540
<i>But...</i>

10:56.470 --> 11:04.100
It's time for the final event in 
our Mixed Disciplines Combat Tournament!

11:04.580 --> 11:08.310
Our last battle will be 
between Seika Lamprogue,

11:08.310 --> 11:10.270
who's certainly lived up to his family name!

11:10.600 --> 11:14.190
How many more secrets does 
he have in store for us?

11:14.740 --> 11:17.830
Then there's the strange man with the 
strange hair and strange ways

11:17.830 --> 11:20.130
who's drawn the most 
attention at this tournament!

11:20.130 --> 11:24.450
The Rugrock Merchants Association's secret
weapon, the evil eye slaughterer, Kyle!

11:24.450 --> 11:27.330
Hey. Sorry it's me and not Mabel.

11:27.760 --> 11:28.980
Mabel?

11:28.980 --> 11:32.810
Yes. This is a problem. 
It wasn't what was planned.

11:32.810 --> 11:34.770
Is she alive?

11:34.770 --> 11:35.740
Yup.

11:35.740 --> 11:36.980
I see.

11:36.980 --> 11:38.360
Good.

11:38.360 --> 11:41.720
Then I can kill her.

11:41.980 --> 11:43.880
She's your sister.

11:43.880 --> 11:44.560
Yes.

11:44.560 --> 11:48.700
The last of our group. My beloved sister.

11:48.700 --> 11:51.060
But I was told to kill her.

11:51.330 --> 11:53.950
You weren't that way before.

11:53.950 --> 11:56.150
Have you forgotten that?

11:56.450 --> 11:58.480
Why do you care?

11:58.480 --> 12:00.320
It's none of your business.

12:00.320 --> 12:02.390
'Cause I don't like it.

12:02.390 --> 12:04.870
She's your only sister. 
Take good care of her.

12:05.330 --> 12:09.440
When you lose this fight, I think 
I'll have you apologize to Mabel.

12:09.440 --> 12:11.710
Why do you think I'll lose to you?

12:12.120 --> 12:14.040
Let the battle begin!

12:14.380 --> 12:17.290
Summoning. Onbonoyasu.

12:19.880 --> 12:22.120
I can't see a thing that's 
going on down there!

12:22.120 --> 12:23.970
What's happening?

12:26.750 --> 12:28.930
I guess that's not enough 
to throw you off your game.

12:28.930 --> 12:30.260
<i>Phase of fire and earth.</i>

12:30.260 --> 12:31.420
<i>Spell of Ghostlight.</i>

12:38.260 --> 12:39.570
<i>How about this, then?</i>

12:40.530 --> 12:44.150
<i>Phase of wood and metal. 
Spell of Mercury Binding Vines.</i>

12:46.240 --> 12:47.390
<i>Are we done?</i>

12:57.170 --> 13:00.000
It's no fun getting no reaction at all.

13:04.950 --> 13:07.220
Summoning. Ushioni.

13:12.180 --> 13:16.560
You've lost your emotions. Does that 
really make you a perfect soldier?

13:16.560 --> 13:18.330
A minotaur?

13:21.320 --> 13:25.200
I don't think feeling terror is a bad thing.

13:31.660 --> 13:34.830
He's on a whole different level than you.

13:34.830 --> 13:40.210
If you had it in you to feel fear, 
you'd know better than to fight him.

13:40.640 --> 13:42.280
You held back, right?

13:46.270 --> 13:48.700
You're actually leaving him alive, huh?

13:48.700 --> 13:49.430
Am I being naive?

13:49.800 --> 13:50.990
You are.

13:50.990 --> 13:54.320
But I'm starting to think that's okay.

13:56.140 --> 13:57.470
A spell seal?

13:57.470 --> 13:58.480
Oh, no!

14:08.200 --> 14:10.960
<i>The barrier's working. So why?</i>

14:10.960 --> 14:14.440
<i>Did it damage him somehow when 
it first started infecting him?</i>

14:15.050 --> 14:16.080
What do I erase...

14:16.400 --> 14:17.750
<i>Will I make it in time?</i>

14:19.740 --> 14:24.840
You told me to apologize to Mabel, right?

14:25.530 --> 14:28.510
Tell her, please...

14:33.880 --> 14:37.600
So you'd try to beat me at curses?

14:39.630 --> 14:42.060
<i>You're going to regret that.</i>

14:43.480 --> 14:47.360
<i>It's fine. The vessel 
hasn't been that damaged.</i>

14:47.360 --> 14:49.290
<i>I can use a substitute to repair it.</i>

14:50.400 --> 14:51.450
<i>Yes...</i>

14:51.450 --> 14:53.740
<i>In my last life, I was the strongest.</i>

14:53.740 --> 14:56.160
<i>If I want to bring the 
dead back to life, I can!</i>

14:59.250 --> 15:00.900
On apaakuroti.

15:00.900 --> 15:02.620
Padaarusu sam disshuti.

15:00.900 --> 15:02.620
No, Seika!

15:02.620 --> 15:04.420
Adounike ishutika.

15:02.620 --> 15:04.420
That spell will make you stand out too much!

15:04.810 --> 15:08.090
You said you were going to 
hide your power in this life!

15:08.090 --> 15:11.430
Did you forget why you had to reincarnate?

15:14.600 --> 15:17.100
Please, don't do this!

15:17.100 --> 15:23.400
Do you owe this man any debt that would 
make you have to do this for him?

15:23.680 --> 15:25.690
I know how you feel...

15:25.690 --> 15:27.570
I know that...

15:28.740 --> 15:32.870
you're kinder than anyone else.

15:35.660 --> 15:37.410
<i>The tournament ended.</i>

15:37.710 --> 15:40.930
<i>I told everyone that 
the reason Kyle disappeared</i>

15:40.930 --> 15:45.090
<i>was that I destroyed him 
without leaving a trace.</i>

15:45.090 --> 15:47.760
<i>In the end, the Emperor never showed.</i>

15:47.760 --> 15:50.730
<i>The tournament committee 
gave me the victory medal.</i>

15:50.730 --> 15:54.510
<i>Of course, I politely declined 
to join the Royal Guards.</i>

15:54.860 --> 15:59.920
<i>The only thing that did work out in my 
favor was that I got the prize money.</i>

16:01.200 --> 16:04.850
<i>I moved Kyle's body into another 
phase of space to carry it out.</i>

16:05.360 --> 16:07.850
<i>I wanted to, at least, bury him.</i>

16:08.750 --> 16:09.750
Mabel...

16:09.750 --> 16:10.800
It's okay.

16:10.800 --> 16:12.050
I knew this would happen.

16:12.730 --> 16:16.240
I guessed that my brother had been cursed.

16:16.240 --> 16:18.080
So don't worry about it.

16:18.080 --> 16:22.040
I'd given up on even being 
able to say goodbye to him.

16:22.760 --> 16:25.760
So Mabel is your actual name, then.

16:26.680 --> 16:28.790
Yes. But how...?

16:28.790 --> 16:32.050
He kept calling your name.

16:32.480 --> 16:33.280
So...

16:33.750 --> 16:34.720
I see.

16:34.970 --> 16:39.430
He actually gave me a message for you.

16:40.660 --> 16:43.980
I didn't know what it meant, though.

16:43.980 --> 16:46.740
He said he was sorry about 
the four-leaf clover.

16:50.240 --> 16:52.280
A little before the surgery,

16:52.280 --> 16:59.240
my brother accidentally broke a four-leaf 
clover hairpin that I really liked.

16:59.830 --> 17:02.930
We got into a little tiff over it.

17:03.550 --> 17:05.850
I think that's what he meant...

17:07.000 --> 17:09.040
It was nothing, though...

17:11.800 --> 17:15.470
Episode 7:
Brother and Sister

17:17.690 --> 17:20.560
What happens to me now?

17:20.560 --> 17:24.850
I told you. 
You're going back to school to study.

17:24.850 --> 17:25.640
Really?

17:25.640 --> 17:27.840
Yeah. It'll be fine.

17:27.840 --> 17:31.070
I'll take care of things, 
so don't worry about it.

17:31.520 --> 17:33.060
Now, let's go.

17:37.570 --> 17:38.910
They're finally back!

17:39.190 --> 17:43.330
<i>After the tournament, I told the 
two of them most of what happened.</i>

17:43.330 --> 17:46.690
<i>Not about the hero, though.</i>

17:46.690 --> 17:49.710
<i>I didn't want Amyu knowing yet.</i>

17:50.570 --> 17:51.820
Welcome back.

17:51.820 --> 17:53.460
I was tired of waiting.

17:53.460 --> 17:55.010
Sorry, sorry.

17:55.010 --> 17:56.090
Wait.

17:56.390 --> 17:57.930
Fight me.

17:58.380 --> 18:00.660
No. I don't feel like it.

18:00.660 --> 18:02.310
Just fight me.

18:02.310 --> 18:03.920
These aren't practice swords.

18:03.920 --> 18:06.640
So you lose if your weapon 
breaks or you drop it.

18:06.640 --> 18:09.100
And no magic this time.

18:09.100 --> 18:10.430
Sure, but...

18:10.430 --> 18:11.960
I get to use it, though.

18:11.960 --> 18:13.650
Are you joking?

18:13.650 --> 18:14.700
It's only fair, isn't it?

18:14.700 --> 18:16.570
Since you won once.

18:16.570 --> 18:18.010
Give me a handicap.

18:18.010 --> 18:20.240
Seika, give the signal.

18:20.240 --> 18:21.500
Err, okay.

18:21.500 --> 18:23.490
Okay... begin!

18:26.000 --> 18:27.040
<i>She's slower than before?</i>

18:35.760 --> 18:37.340
I win!

18:37.340 --> 18:38.900
Well, new girl?

18:38.900 --> 18:42.510
I can do the same trick with gravity magic.

18:42.510 --> 18:46.220
I'm top of my class in all elements! 
Don't mess with me!

18:46.490 --> 18:49.350
What? Did you just want to brag?

18:49.350 --> 18:54.010
You wanted to beat your 
brother yourself, didn't you?

18:54.010 --> 18:57.360
It wasn't about winning or losing. I just...

18:57.360 --> 18:58.310
You're lying.

18:58.310 --> 19:00.200
I can tell by the way you swing your sword.

19:00.200 --> 19:03.920
You definitely weren't the 
quiet type of little sister,

19:03.920 --> 19:06.450
who's always hiding behind her big brother.

19:06.450 --> 19:10.620
You were trying to prove you 
were better than him. Right?

19:11.150 --> 19:15.940
And the reason you entered the tournament 
was that it was your last chance to do so.

19:15.940 --> 19:17.960
Don't act like you understand!

19:18.510 --> 19:19.800
What are you trying to say?

19:19.800 --> 19:22.220
Now you can try and beat me.

19:23.180 --> 19:24.860
We've both won one and lost one.

19:24.860 --> 19:28.880
I was getting bored because I didn't 
have a training partner at school.

19:28.880 --> 19:30.230
Practice with me for a while.

19:32.800 --> 19:34.080
This is stupid.

19:37.190 --> 19:40.400
U-Um, shouldn't we get going?

19:41.010 --> 19:42.730
Yeah, let's go home.

19:46.880 --> 19:49.500
So, what did you want to talk about?

19:49.500 --> 19:53.520
I saved the life of your fake hero, Mabel's, life.

19:53.520 --> 19:55.040
Satisfied?

19:55.510 --> 19:58.250
You figured all that out, huh?

19:58.250 --> 19:59.990
Yes, that's right.

19:59.990 --> 20:05.060
Mabel was our way of hiding 
Amyu from the demons.

20:05.060 --> 20:11.250
But Rugrock sold her to you, 
instead of lending her, right?

20:11.250 --> 20:15.040
It makes no sense that they'd ask for her 
back if she was supposed to die

20:15.040 --> 20:16.310
in the final round.

20:16.650 --> 20:20.600
They thought Kyle would kill her.

20:20.600 --> 20:26.700
But your plan was for me to win 
and bring her back to the school.

20:27.150 --> 20:31.200
Yes. They had this whole 
thing planned out carefully.

20:31.200 --> 20:35.880
They wanted Kyle to win in the tournament 
to make their mercenaries famous.

20:36.180 --> 20:38.750
They saw us as tools, and nothing more.

20:39.990 --> 20:48.270
But instead, thanks to you, we got Mabel 
and they lost their masterpiece, Kyle.

20:48.920 --> 20:50.310
Serves them right.

20:50.980 --> 20:54.570
You went so far as to increase 
the number of people you could send,

20:54.570 --> 20:57.390
just to make sure I went.

20:57.390 --> 20:58.480
Why?

20:59.140 --> 21:01.650
Because I felt bad for her.

21:01.650 --> 21:03.970
She had such talent,

21:03.970 --> 21:08.450
but a face like she'd been through 
every type of misery imaginable...

21:11.430 --> 21:16.580
She told me that she wanted 
to set her brother free.

21:16.580 --> 21:19.170
She wanted me to send her.

21:19.600 --> 21:22.480
It struck me as wrong.

21:22.480 --> 21:28.390
So I came up with a way to use 
my trump card, Seika Lamprogue,

21:28.390 --> 21:30.720
in a way that would cause 
her to lose but survive.

21:30.720 --> 21:34.640
And you didn't think I would 
lose to Mabel or Kyle?

21:35.000 --> 21:38.180
I've lived a long life.

21:38.180 --> 21:43.030
I can tell how strong someone is.

21:43.360 --> 21:48.180
Regardless, her safety at 
the school is guaranteed.

21:48.180 --> 21:50.990
Then there's nothing for me to do.

21:50.990 --> 21:52.950
What do you mean?

21:52.950 --> 21:57.450
She's starting out at as 
a student at a new school.

21:57.450 --> 21:59.420
She'll need your help,

21:59.820 --> 22:01.780
as an upperclassman.

22:01.780 --> 22:03.850
I'm aware of that.

22:04.520 --> 22:07.830
By the way, you said you'd lived a long life.

22:07.830 --> 22:09.720
How old are you, ma'am?

22:09.720 --> 22:12.190
You're asking me my age?

22:12.190 --> 22:14.280
Such a rude kid.

22:14.280 --> 22:17.270
I stopped counting after 300.

22:22.650 --> 22:23.780
Seika.

22:24.690 --> 22:27.200
Hey. Huh? Where's Mabel?

22:27.530 --> 22:29.700
Her hair color...

22:29.700 --> 22:31.820
She switched it back a long time ago.

22:31.820 --> 22:34.670
Seika, you didn't notice?

22:34.670 --> 22:37.710
Oh, yeah... I noticed... I guess.

22:37.710 --> 22:40.630
You can be dense like that sometimes.

22:41.060 --> 22:42.810
No running.

22:42.810 --> 22:43.770
I need to talk to you.

22:43.770 --> 22:45.380
W-Well, I don't need to talk to you.

22:45.770 --> 22:47.310
Well, I do.

22:47.310 --> 22:49.010
Why didn't you come yesterday?

22:49.430 --> 22:52.750
I don't want to study with you anymore.

22:52.750 --> 22:55.800
You're such a strict teacher!

22:55.800 --> 22:59.480
I have to be. You need to be 
able to keep up with classes,

22:59.480 --> 23:02.690
and right now you can't even 
solve the entrance exam problems.

23:03.040 --> 23:08.920
But... I've never had any 
reason to learn until now.

23:08.920 --> 23:10.110
Mabel...

23:10.500 --> 23:14.030
Being held back a year is something 
that comes to us all equally.

23:14.030 --> 23:16.410
Don't say that like it's some famous saying!

23:16.830 --> 23:20.330
Y-Yifa, help me!

23:20.810 --> 23:22.130
Seika...

23:23.090 --> 23:25.130
I think you're being too easy on her!

23:26.890 --> 23:31.180
So, yeah, Yifa says she'll 
help you study today.

23:35.440 --> 23:38.710
Studying's scary!
